## 2. Data Layer Deep Dive

### `.chezmoi.yaml.tmpl` — The Brain

This single template **generates the final `chezmoi.yaml` config** AND **defines all variables available to every other template**. It runs first, before anything else.

#### Critical Sections

```yaml
# 1. ENVIRONMENT DETECTING (runs at template time)
$ci := or (eq (env "CI") "true") (env "GITHUB_ACTIONS" | not | not) ...
$ephemeral := or $ci $codespaces $devContainer $gitpod $replit
$headless := or (not $interactiveTTY) (not $guiAvailable) $wsl $inContainer $sshSession $termux
$isVps := ... # hostname "instance-*", user "ubuntu", SSH, no GUI
$profile := env "CHEZMOI_PROFILE" | default ($ismanaged | ternary "work" "personal")

# 2. FEATURE FLAGS (hierarchical, overridden by data files)
features:
  ai:
    coding_assistants: true
    hermes:
      dashboard:
        enabled: true
        port: 9119
        domain: "hermes.fabiosouzadev.duckdns.org"

# 3. DIRECTORY PATHS (consolidated for templates)
dirs:
  local: "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.local"
  bin: "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.local/bin"

# 4. CONSOLIDATED DATA OUTPUT (available as `.settings`, `.features`, `.dirs` in all templates)
data:
  settings: { vps: $isVps, ephemeral: $ephemeral, headless: $headless, profile: $profile, ... }
  features: $features
  dirs: $dirs
```

#### Variables Available Everywhere

| Namespace | Contains | Example |
|-----------|----------|---------|
| `.settings` | Environment detection results | `.settings.vps`, `.settings.headless`, `.settings.profile` |
| `.features` | Feature flags hierarchy | `.features.ai.hermes.dashboard.enabled` |
| `.dirs` | Computed paths | `.dirs.bin`, `.dirs.workspaces.zup` |
| `.chezmoi` | Built-in chezmoi vars | `.chezmoi.os`, `.chezmoi.hostname`, `.chezmoi.username` |

### `.chezmoidata/` — Platform-Specific Data

```
.chezmoidata/
├── darwin/           # macOS packages, configs
├── linux/            # Linux distro packages (apt, pacman)
├── windows/          # Windows packages (winget, scoop)
├── termux/           # Android/Termux packages
├── vps/              # VPS-specific features (features.yaml)
├── ai_tools.yaml     # AI tools definitions (npm + curl installers)
├── omniroute.yaml    # OmniRoute config
├── ollama.yaml       # Ollama models
├── idea.yaml         # IntelliJ IDEA versions
└── repos.json        # Git repos to clone (personal/work/other)
```

**Pattern**: Data is **declarative YAML**, logic lives in scripts. This enables:
- Easy auditing (what packages per OS?)
- CI validation (schema check YAML)
- Platform-specific overrides without template logic

### `repos.json` — Workspace Declaration

```json
{
  "personal": [{"repo": "git@github.com:user/repo.git", "path": "my-project"}],
  "work": {
    "workplaces": {
      "Zup": [{"repo": "git@gitlab.zup.com.br:team/project.git", "path": "project"}]
    }
  },
  "other": [{"repo": "https://github.com/other/repo.git", "path": "forks/other"}]
}
```

Used by `run_onchange_after_605-clone-my-repos.sh.tmpl` to bootstrap workspaces.

