## 6. Secret Management

### Two Systems Coexist

| System | Use Case | Files |
|--------|----------|-------|
| **age (chezmoi native)** | Modern, primary | `private_dot_ssh/`, `private_dot_hermes/`, `private_dot_config/private_systemd/`, `.chezmoi.yaml.tmpl` (recipient) |
| **GPG (legacy)** | Encrypted Zsh snippets | `dot_zshrc.d/encrypted_*.zsh.asc` |

### Age Configuration (in `.chezmoi.yaml.tmpl`)

```yaml
encryption: gpg  # chezmoi uses gpg CLI to call age

gpg:
  recipient: E691C031009FB1DAA3A25125212D516F623C5747
  args: [--quiet]
```

**Identity file**: `~/.config/chezmoi/key.txt` (age private key)

### Adding a New Secret

```bash
# 1. Place plaintext file in source
chezmoi add --encrypt ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

# 2. ChezMoi encrypts with age (using recipient pubkey)
# 3. Stores in source as private_dot_ssh/id_ed25519 (encrypted)
# 4. On apply: decrypts → ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 (600 perms)
```

### Fork Safety (Critical)

> **NEVER fork this repo without rotating the age key.**

```bash
# On new machine / fork:
age-keygen -o ~/.config/chezmoi/key.txt
# Update recipient in .chezmoi.yaml.tmpl
# Re-encrypt all secrets:
chezmoi re-add --encrypt ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 ~/.config/chezmoi/key.txt ...
```

