## 8. Step-by-Step: Analyzing a New ChezMoi Repo

### Phase 1: Orientation (5 min)

```bash
# 1. Find source directory
cat .chezmoiroot          # Usually "home" or "."

# 2. Read the brain
cat home/.chezmoi.yaml.tmpl | head -200

# 3. List structure
find home -type f -name "*.tmpl" | sort
```

### Phase 2: Data Flow Mapping (15 min)

```bash
# 1. Environment detection variables
grep -n "ephemeral\|headless\|vps\|profile" home/.chezmoi.yaml.tmpl

# 2. Feature flags
grep -n "features:" home/.chezmoi.yaml.tmpl -A 50

# 3. Data files
ls -la home/.chezmoidata/
cat home/.chezmoidata/ai_tools.yaml
```

### Phase 3: Script Inventory (10 min)

```bash
# 1. List all scripts with order
find home/.chezmoiscripts -name "*.tmpl" | sort -V

# 2. Check guards usage
grep -r "script_is_not_ephemeral\|script_is_not_headless" home/.chezmoiscripts/

# 3. Identify onchange scripts (re-run on config change)
find home/.chezmoiscripts -name "run_onchange_*"
```

### Phase 4: Template Patterns (10 min)

```bash
# 1. Ignore patterns (what's excluded where)
cat home/.chezmoiignore.tmpl

# 2. Common templates (guards, helpers)
ls -la home/.chezmoitemplates/common/

# 3. Encrypted files
find home -name "private_*" -o -name "encrypted_*"
```

### Phase 5: Secret & Profile Audit (5 min)

```bash
# 1. Age recipient
grep "recipient:" home/.chezmoi.yaml.tmpl

# 2. Profile detection logic
grep -n "profile\|ismanaged\|isVps\|workplace" home/.chezmoi.yaml.tmpl

# 3. External deps
ls -la home/.chezmoiexternals/
```

